    "narrative": "The Austin Waves enter today\u2019s slate with **Gunnar Henderson** as the clear primary anchor; his 83.29 score is driven by an ideal convergence of favorable park factors, a weak 4.56 xERA matchup against Buehler, and a significant boost from wind conditions. **Jackson Merrill** (71.85), **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (71.38), **Kyle Tucker** (71.33), and **Andy Pages** (70.21) also qualify as elite options. Both **Jackson Merrill** and **Andy Pages** gain notable utility today due to their ability to exploit a slow pitcher delivery, providing that critical premium on stolen base potential that remains the focal point of our aggressive, speed-oriented roster strategy.\n\nManaging our bench remains a high-wire act, particularly with the roster strain caused by injuries to **Luis Robert Jr.** and **Jordan Westburg**. The decision to start **Wade Meckler** (49.40) over **Miguel Vargas** (45.42) was the tightest call on the board. While **Miguel Vargas** holds a respectable projection, **Wade Meckler** secured the utility spot by virtue of his higher-order batting position (3rd vs 2nd), which provides better opportunities for counting stats. Meanwhile, **Liam Hicks** (42.69) faces an uphill battle against the elite Skenes; while he remains in the lineup for game-cap preservation, he is the most volatile asset today, as any deviation from his aggressive approach against such high-velocity pitching could tank his efficiency rating quickly.",
